Theme decided by Hermes: 'Larimar / Caribbean Blue'. Signature material is Dominican blue pectolite (larimar) associated with Barahona. Sources discovered: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larimar and https://www.dominican-larimar.com/index.php/en/the-story-of-larimar/ (latter commercial source; label). Search reports blue/blue-green mineral from Barahona; fetch actual source via Python urllib or browser if feasible, save small factual research notes/URLs. No copied imagery, sacred motifs or claims of authentic stone. Written research-backed design-brief.md BEFORE modeling is the primary concept reference, not invented previous approved art.
Design decisions: wide keepsake silhouette approx 3.72 x 2.38 and 1.9 body height, existing inherited pivots/interior/brass mechanical language. Body polished pale cyan/sky blue larimar-inspired stone with irregular white cellular veining, darker blue pockets; not horizontal cedar grain. Narrow dark teal seam. Lid framed brass and polished blue stone with a raised organic larimar cabochon/cluster on a low asymmetric coastal-white stone setting: sculptural mineral ornament, NOT geographical replica or glacier. Ornament entirely lid-owned, modest max 0.55 height above lid, clearly readable mobile. Hollow liner. Retain exactly staged 80deg latch release then 105deg lid opening and inherited pivots; sample all moving meshes for collision with only explicit bearing exclusions.

Produce editable named .blend, GLB, procedural compact color/roughness/normal maps, reproducible Python Blender authoring; standalone offline HTML strictly <5000000 bytes (all assets/runtime embedded), actual source-rendered poster, rotation/open/close/reset/reduced-motion, desktop+mobile file:// browser evidence, source-check/parity-check/motion/browser/delivery checks and README honest limits. Reuse mechanical/viewer/test infrastructure, not cedar artwork. Audit all UI copy. Script names expected: maps.py, author.py, build.py, verify_source.py, verify_parity.py, verify_browser.py, verify_extended.py, test_theme.py, package_delivery.py (adapt where necessary). Package only in this directory (no external output writes). Include .gitattributes '* -text'. Preserve true failed check logs then fix root causes, do not weaken gates. At least one explicit negative control to show gates reject defects. Inspect generated images if available.

Blender C:/Users/futur/AppData/Local/Programs/Blender-5.2.1/blender.exe --background --factory-startup --python-exit-code 1 --python SCRIPT. Bound render threads to 2, samples 24-32, 1000x800 or smaller; disable compositor/denoising if memory contention; check nonblack/alpha coverage. python available, python3 missing. Three/esbuild reuse sibling node_modules. Actual glTF roughness is green channel. Blender source parity needs float tolerance. All collisions include new ornaments. Archive inventory needs explicit required artifacts + SHA256 readback. Browser uses Python Playwright installed Edge; desktop/mobile emulation not real phone proof. Sync reduced-motion/reset state to frames or synchronous input, not unbounded sleeps.

You may run all above build/tests and should return concise files changed, exact byte counts, tests commands/results and known limitations. Hermes will independently rerun build/source/parity/browser/theme/delivery after reviewing diff. Stop when bounded complete; do not extend scope.
